I used comma operator in pond lily pads: `c.beginPath(), c.ellipse(...), c.fill();` — valid but ugly. Fine.

Now drawBuildings rewrite. Let me replace the whole function with richer detail. I need to keep the building's `club`, `garage`, `pool`, `name`, `neon` behavior.

Design:

```js
function drawBuildings(c) {
  for (const b of buildings) {
    const x=b.x*T, y=b.y*T, w=b.w*T, h=b.h*T;
    const p=b.pal, seed=b.seed;
    const tall = h > 90;
    // shadow
    c.fillStyle='rgba(8,6,18,.45)'; c.fillRect(x+8,y+9,w,h);
    // outer base/walls
    c.fillStyle=p.wall2; c.fillRect(x,y,w,h);
    c.fillStyle='rgba(255,255,255,.10)'; c.fillRect(x,y,w,2);
    // roof
    c.fillStyle=p.roof; c.fillRect(x+3,y+3,w-6,h-6);
    // roof tiles / concrete panels
    c.fillStyle='rgba(0,0,0,.06)';
    for (let ry=y+3; ry<y+h-6; ry+=9) c.fillRect(x+3,ry,w-6,1);
    for (let rx=x+3; rx<x+w-6; rx+=9) c.fillRect(rx,y+3,1,h-6);
    // edge highlight
    c.fillStyle='rgba(255,255,255,.08)'; c.fillRect(x+3,y+3,w-6,1);
    // roof details
    // AC units (2)
    const acN = w>70 && h>60 ? 2 : 1;
    for (let i=0;i<acN;i++){
      const ax = x + 8 + (seed*37 + i*53) % Math.max(10, w-30);
      const ay = y + 10 + (seed*29 + i*41) % Math.max(10, h-40);
      c.fillStyle='rgba(20,18,28,.25)'; c.fillRect(ax+2, ay+2, 14, 10);
      c.fillStyle='#8a8f9a'; c.fillRect(ax, ay, 14, 10);
      c.fillStyle='#b9bec7'; c.fillRect(ax+1, ay+1, 12, 3);
      c.strokeStyle='#5c6069'; c.lineWidth=1; c.beginPath(); c.arc(ax+7, ay+7, 3, 0, TAU); c.stroke();
      c.fillStyle='#5c6069'; c.fillRect(ax+6, ay+4, 2, 6); c.fillRect(ax+4, ay+6, 6, 2);
    }
    // water tank or antenna based on seed
    if (seed > .62 && w > 50) { ... circle tank ... }
    if (seed < .35 && w > 40) { antenna with light }
    // skylight / solar
    if (seed > .45 && w > 60) { solar panel }
    // rooftop garden
    if (seed > .8 && h > 70) { green patch }
    // side windows (left/right edges)
    // facade at bottom
    const facadeH = 11;
    c.fillStyle = p.wall2; c.fillRect(x, y+h-facadeH, w, facadeH);
    c.fillStyle = p.wall; c.fillRect(x+1, y+h-facadeH+1, w-2, facadeH-2);
    // grime
    // windows along facade
    for (let wx=x+6; wx<x+w-8; wx+=12) {
      const lit = hash2(wx, y) > .4;
      c.fillStyle = lit ? '#ffe8a8' : '#302c3b';
      c.fillRect(wx, y+h-facadeH+3, 7, 5);
      c.fillStyle = 'rgba(255,255,255,.18)'; c.fillRect(wx, y+h-facadeH+3, 7, 1);
      // sill
      c.fillStyle = p.trim; c.fillRect(wx-1, y+h-facadeH+8, 9, 1);
    }
    // door
    c.fillStyle='#1d1626'; c.fillRect(x+w/2-6, y+h-8, 12, 8);
    c.fillStyle=p.trim; c.fillRect(x+w/2-9, y+h-11, 18, 3);
    // awning stripes above windows for shops
    if (b.name && w>50) { ... striped awning ... }
    // neon underglow for named
    if (b.neon) { c.fillStyle=b.neon + '55'; c.fillRect(x+2,y+h-1,w-4,1); ... }
    // balconies for tall
    // rooftop club / pool / garage special
  }
}
```

Need to be careful with the sign positions: signs are drawn at y = b.y + b.h - .15 tiles = bottom of building. Night layer draws text there. Facade is bottom 11px. Good.

Add club-specific neon strip at bottom; garage door already; pool existing.

Also add "roof access" stairs.

Let me write the full replacement. Avoid using `b.neon + '55'` if neon is null. Fine.

Also windows on side edges: for tall buildings, draw small windows along left/right vertical edges with lit colors.

I'll include an awning with alternating stripes using p.trim and a dark color, only for named buildings or small shops.

