But addTrash at x=7 may be near world edge (x=7*16=112) fine.

Placement y should avoid crosswalk intersections? Sidewalk at x=27 across y; intersections at y=26..28 etc. If y falls in road intersection y=26..28, then x=27 is road (since horizontal road spans all x? Actually HROADS y=26..28, and for all x, setTile road if h; yes x=27 becomes road). So skip if tileAt not SIDEWALK/GRASS. We can check `if (tileAt(tx,ty) !== TILE.SIDEWALK) continue;` after world generated. But sidewalk conversion only for x<100 and grass; if x=27 and y in road, tile is ROAD. So skip.

