Maybe add a "beach boardwalk" with shops/arcade and a second pier with ferris wheel on the beach. We already have ferris at arcade and beach stalls. Fine.

Now, let's consider adding a new tile type? No.

Add more texture on building facades: neon signs with text already at night; during day, signs are only drawn in night layer (not visible in day!). The night layer is drawn only when nf > .02; since start tod 0.70 nf=0, so signs (neon text) are invisible during daytime. In the gate screenshot, gate signs are visible because they're props. But building name signs (from signs array) are only in night layer, so not visible at day. That's a detail issue. We should draw signs in the world canvas too (not only night). Currently buildNightLayer draws them; but the world canvas doesn't. Add sign text to drawBuildings or a separate drawSigns(c) called in buildWorld. That would make the city more detailed and legible during day.

Add `drawSigns(c)` function that draws text with a dark backing and colored text at each sign position, then call in buildWorld before props. But night layer also draws the same signs; at night it will overlay, fine.

Implementation:

```js
function drawSigns(c) {
  c.save();
  c.textAlign='center'; c.textBaseline='middle';
  for (const s of signs) {
    const w = Math.max(30, s.text.length * 6 + 8);
    c.fillStyle='rgba(12,8,18,.85)';
    c.fillRect(s.x - w/2, s.y - 9, w, 12);
    c.strokeStyle=s.color; c.lineWidth=1; c.strokeRect(...);
    c.font='6px PressStart, monospace';
    c.fillStyle=s.color;
    c.fillText(s.text, s.x, s.y - 3);
  }
  c.restore();
}
```

But sign.y is b.y + b.h - .15 tiles => at bottom edge of building, which is facade. The sign text would be over the facade/awning. Good.

Also maybe add rooftop billboards? no.

Call `drawSigns(c)` in buildWorld after drawBuildings, before drawProps. Need to define function. Add after drawBuildings.

Let's do it.

